  [1mThe main problem:[0m a user ID is usually something login [3mreturns[0m, not something you pass in. Before someone logs in, the
  client doesn't know who they are, so the form has no [38;5;153muserId[39m to hand to [38;5;153mlogin()[39m. A [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter only makes sense
  if it comes from somewhere I haven't found. Your answer changes the whole design:

